## ✅ Phase 5: InvalidationProvider Event Bus Integration - COMPLETE

### Objective
Connect InvalidationProvider to domain event bus for automatic cache invalidation across the application.

**STATUS: COMPLETED ✅ (Jan 23, 2026)**

### Current State Analysis
```typescript
// InvalidationProvider - LOCAL ONLY
const invalidate = useCallback((key: string) => {
    const callbacks = subscribersRef.current.get(key);
    // Triggers local callbacks only
}, []);

// InMemoryEventBus - SEPARATE SYSTEM
async publish<T extends DomainEvent>(event: T): Promise<void> {
    // Publishes to domain handlers
    // NOT connected to React invalidation
}
```

### Implementation Plan

#### 5.1: Research Domain Events (30 mins) ✅ COMPLETE
**Tasks:**
- [x] Map all DomainEvent types in core package
- [x] Identify which events should trigger cache invalidation
- [x] Document event-to-query-key mapping

**Expected Events:**
- SpaceCreatedEvent → invalidate 'spaces'
- SpaceDeletedEvent → invalidate 'spaces'
- SpaceRenamedEvent → invalidate 'spaces'
- SpaceUpdatedEvent → invalidate 'spaces'
- ItemCreatedEvent → invalidate 'space-items'
- ItemDeletedEvent → invalidate 'space-items', 'pinned-items'
- ItemMovedEvent → invalidate 'space-items'
- ItemRenamedEvent → invalidate 'space-items'
- ItemPinnedEvent → invalidate 'pinned-items'
- ItemUnpinnedEvent → invalidate 'pinned-items'

**Files to Check:**
- `packages/core/src/domain/events/`
- `packages/core/src/domain/events/DomainEvent.ts`

#### 5.2: Create Event-to-Invalidation Bridge (1 hour) ✅ COMPLETE
**File:** `packages/react-ui/src/hooks/common/EventBusIntegration.ts`

```typescript
import { useEffect, useRef } from 'react';
import { serviceRegistry, SERVICE_KEYS } from '@spayce/infrastructure';
import type { IEventBus, DomainEvent } from '@spayce/core';
import { useInvalidation } from './InvalidationContext';

export function useEventBusInvalidation() {
    const { invalidate } = useInvalidation();
    const eventBusRef = useRef<IEventBus | null>(null);

    useEffect(() => {
        // Get event bus from service registry
        eventBusRef.current = serviceRegistry.get<IEventBus>(SERVICE_KEYS.EVENT_BUS);

        // Map events to invalidation keys
        const eventHandlers = {
            'space.created': () => invalidate('spaces'),
            'space.deleted': () => invalidate('spaces'),
            'space.renamed': () => invalidate('spaces'),
            'space.updated': () => invalidate('spaces'),
            'item.created': () => {
                invalidate('space-items');
                invalidate('recent-items');
            },
            'item.deleted': () => {
                invalidate('space-items');
                invalidate('pinned-items');
                invalidate('recent-items');
            },
            'item.moved': () => invalidate('space-items'),
            'item.renamed': () => invalidate('space-items'),
            'item.pinned': () => invalidate('pinned-items'),
            'item.unpinned': () => invalidate('pinned-items'),
            'item.reordered': () => invalidate('space-items'),
            'pins.reordered': () => invalidate('pinned-items'),
        };

        // Subscribe to all events
        Object.entries(eventHandlers).forEach(([eventType, handler]) => {
            eventBusRef.current?.subscribe(eventType, async () => {
                handler();
            });
        });

        // Cleanup not needed - event bus persists for app lifetime
    }, [invalidate]);
}
```

#### 5.3: Update InvalidationProvider (30 mins) ✅ COMPLETE
**File:** `packages/react-ui/src/hooks/common/InvalidationContext.tsx`

**Changes:**
- Add useEventBusInvalidation() call in InvalidationProvider
- Ensure it's called at provider level, not in every hook

```typescript
export function InvalidationProvider({ children }: InvalidationProviderProps): React.ReactElement {
    const subscribersRef = useRef<Map<string, Set<InvalidationCallback>>>(new Map());
    
    // ... existing subscribe/invalidate logic ...
    
    // NEW: Connect to event bus
    useEventBusInvalidation();
    
    return (
        <InvalidationContext.Provider value={{ subscribe, invalidate }}>
            {children}
        </InvalidationContext.Provider>
    );
}
```

